s libsndfile-1.2.2.tar.xz etc.\",\n      \"applicability\": \"FACT: coherent release pin for the I/O boundary.\",\n      \"relation\": \"dynamic_fields_differ (download counters; tag and dates identical to research capture b9ed5f48...)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S14\",\n      \"title\": \"libsamplerate documentation: Full API (api_full.html)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://libsndfile.github.io/libsamplerate/api_full.html\",\n      \"pin\": \"docs at capture; library latest release 0.2.2\",\n      \"capture_id\": \"c21768795b444267b1361df10b23d3f6\",\n      \"capture_sha256\": \"b45438c450036c2cc40dd7e8c39abeafa99c1b60e1abb4d993fb6f576beaee85\",\n      \"bytes\": 11230,\n      \"locator\": \"SRC_DATA fields input_frames_used / output_frames_gen; data_in and data_out may not overlap; can be called over and over again with each new call providing new input data; src_reset should be called whenever a converter is used on two separate, unrelated pieces of audio; src_set_ratio smooth transition versus step response; src_clone\",\n      \"applicability\": \"FACT: streaming resampler contract the chunked renderer must follow.\",\n      \"relation\": \"identical_bytes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S15\",\n      \"title\": \"libsamplerate release 0.2.2 (GitHub releases/latest)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/libsndfile/libsamplerate/releases/latest\",\n      \"pin\": \"tag 0.2.2; published 2021-09-05; latest release\",\n      \"capture_id\": \"a5980e3933d34c5a8a8877bf3dd68694\",\n      \"capture_sha256\": \"387d7414b19082b166b4a349f27b03449df1045635f454fdaad915834da0aacf\",\n      \"bytes\": 11779,\n      \"locator\": \"tag_name=0.2.2; published_at 2021-09-05T11:50:41Z; body lists build-system fixes\",\n      \"applicability\": \"FACT: coherent release pin for the resampler.\",\n      \"relation\": \"dynamic_fields_differ (download counters; tag and dates identical to research capture 02251e80...)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S16\",\n      \"title\": \"Audacity Manual: Managing Audacity Projects\",\n      \"url\": \"https://manual.audacityteam.org/man/audacity_projects.html\",\n      \"pin\": \"page last-modified 2026-09-03; captured 2026-10-06T05:48:02Z\",\n      \"capture_id\": \"172d7ac06455484aa72c5a4dc11ab388\",\n      \"capture_sha256\": \"c04277b228960d4c65aafef1b41605ea40ae79affc779232a17704236d5ed5c3\",\n      \"bytes\": 37614,\n      \"range_hashes\": \"first 32768 bytes: d092b77bd6b22ffd5800bc5c27a20edeb6e6d6fcaf548869a52f89b62a7f756e (identical to the research-stage delivered range; all cited statements fall inside it)\",\n      \"locator\": \"a project is stored in a file with an aup3 extension; can be opened and used only by Audacity; the Undo history is not saved with the project; FAT/FAT32 blocked due to 4GB file limit; Automatic Crash Recovery; compaction on close; references the original audio material until you actually perform some kind of edit; edit retains old plus changed audio (doubling); nondestructive trim hides audio causing project bloat, no permanent-delete command; Temporary work files WAL and SHM, deleted on closure, do not move while open\",\n      \"applicability\": \"FACT (product-documented behavior): precedent lessons for project format, recovery, and nondestructive storage costs.\",\n      \"relation\": \"range_identical\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S17\",\n      \"title\": \"SQLite documentation: Atomic Commit In SQLite\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sqlite.org/atomiccommit.html\",\n      \"pin\": \"page last-modified 2026-09-11; captured 2026-10-06T05:48:23Z\",\n      \"capture_id\": \"01f7130bb7c44dd29df8f064cdcabbf1\",\n      \"capture_sha256\": \"5a5be7b660217c9408c8a81eaf2faa2d08832ed3790f895a0a713916ad856ea1\",\n      \"bytes\": 77968,\n      \"range_hashes\": \"first 32768 bytes: 204cdfe22e90a7933f18a2b74558c90ff12997dd22f16facd6bed4f1885bfc10 (identical to research delivered range; cited sections inside it)\",\n      \"locator\": \"section 3.5 rollback journal holds original pages; sections 3.7 and 3.10 two flush/fsync phases; section 3.11 the rollback journal file is deleted, this is the instant where the transaction commits, journal existence decides commit versus rollback; section 2 hardware assumptions (writes may be reordered; fsync assumed working); section 4.2 hot rollback journals\",\n      \"applicability\": \"FACT (mechanism family): journal-then-rename/fsync discipline for safe saves and interrupted-save recovery.\",\n      \"relation\": \"identical_bytes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S18\",\n      \"title\": \"W3C WebVTT: The Web Video Text Tracks Format (TR)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.w3.org/TR/webvtt1/\",\n      \"pin\": \"W3C Candidate Recommendation Draft, 20 May 2026; revision 064802512ff9d8cd22dea4aea2cd1508aa2cc679\",\n      \"capture_id\": \"b2e4144e2f904b8fad0e9f59d5de9ae1\",\n      \"capture_sha256\": \"a9425c5bacb46e4f84dc377bfd5366a4c75343dbc8c8b606290bfe065cf0865c\",\n      \"bytes\": 524288,\n      \"capture_note\": \"TR page exceeds the capture cap: body_complete=false; only header/status/abstract relied on, as in the research stage\",\n      \"locator\": \"header: title, W3C Candidate Recommendation Draft 20 May 2026; abstract: captions or subtitles, chapters for content navigation, and more generally any form of metadata that is time-aligned with audio or video content\",\n      \"applicability\": \"FACT: WebVTT is a standardized time-aligned text-track format suited to cue-table interchange; deeper syntax sections UNPINNED (lead L02).\",\n      \"relation\": \"identical_bytes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S19\",\n      \"title\": \"libsndfile documentation: sf_command (command.html)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://libsndfile.github.io/libsndfile/command.html\",\n      \"pin\": \"docs at capture; last-modified 2026-09-01; page 114337 bytes, first 32768 relied on\",\n      \"capture_id\": \"c9526ac8a12d45baacd2288fb21ca0be\",\n      \"capture_sha256\": \"ee59248c61847bd64291e46ce377e277c9e558eb70dd903c8f8c27bb4abe319e\",\n      \"bytes\": 114337,\n      \"range_hashes\": \"first 32768 bytes: 5d94ed953ff730811ea058d9d07a86dc3cc1f83b94bc285c15978376c0cae163\",\n      \"locator\": \"command table: SFC_GET_BROADCAST_INFO Get the Broadcast Chunk info; SFC_SET_BROADCAST_INFO Set the Broadcast Chunk info; SFC_RF64_AUTO_DOWNGRADE Set auto downgrade from RF64 to WAV; SFC_SET_CLIPPING Control automatic clipping behaviour; SFC_CALC_SIGNAL_MAX involves reading through the whole file\",\n      \"applicability\": \"FACT: bext command interface, RF64 downgrade control, and clipping control exist at the pinned docs; NEW this stage (resolves lead L03 at command level; supports the 7.3 RF64 policy and 7.2 clipping census).\",\n      \"relation\": \"new_this_stage\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"S20\",\n      \"title\": \"libsamplerate documentation: Miscellaneous API (api_misc.html)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://libsndfile.github.io/libsamplerate/api_misc.html\",\n      \"pin\": \"docs at capture; last-modified 2026-08-13\",\n      \"capture_id\": \"636ca977cf824523b8e8514e2b76f411\",\n      \"capture_sha256\": \"cbb39118af1b3992455a7742d641693471db1e534350a4f11d827ee4590ef31e\",\n      \"bytes\": 12066,\n      \"locator\": \"converter enum SRC_SINC_BEST_QUALITY=0, SRC_SINC_MEDIUM_QUALITY=1, SRC_SINC_FASTEST=2, SRC_ZERO_ORDER_HOLD=3, SRC_LINEAR=4; SRC_SINC_MEDIUM_QUALITY SNR 97 dB bandwidth 90 percent; src_ratio equals output sample rate over input sample rate; end_of_input 0 if more input, 1 if last buffer; input_frames_used and output_frames_gen are per-call\",\n      \"applicability\": \"FACT: pins the export resampler-quality constant and streaming semantics; NEW this stage.\",\n      \"relation\": \"new_this_stage\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}, "witnesses.json": {"text_utf8": "{\n  \"schema\": \"er9.final.witnesses.v1\",\n  \"stage\": \"critic_final\",\n  \"labels\": {\n    \"executed_by_candidate\": \"Candidate-authored check run in the admitted isolated python_execute sandbox during this critic_final stage; receipted by the runtime. Isolated component check only; does NOT establish full application behavior.\",\n    \"disclosed_failure\": \"A receipt whose output shows FAILED is preserved and disclosed, not hidden; it documents the check process honestly.\",\n    \"adopted_research_stage_receipt\": \"Executed by the research-stage candidate of the same arm; receipts adopted from the frozen research catalog under inputs/prior/. Not re-run in this stage; independently corroborated where noted. Attribution is explicit; no receipt is invented.\",\n    \"proposed_unexecuted\": \"Planned implementation-stage validation; NOT run in any stage so far. No receipt exists.\"\n  },\n  \"witnesses\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FW1\",\n      \"name\": \"Clip/cue mapping arithmetic re-verification and structure result\",\n      \"label\": \"executed_by_candidate\",\n      \"execution_id\": \"exec-0myc811x\",\n      \"completed_utc\": \"2026-10-06T05:49:35Z\",\n      \"exit_code\": 0,\n      \"code_sha256\": \"2a6608d71e5ede57d23d9685cd295b82b8a5453961f145af99352bc614583903\",\n      \"stdout_sha256\": \"d66cfc5f8e2fc79a6122b308016258519ab298f568e8e6608d477fb0a135e721\",\n      \"scope\": \"Floor mapping p(s) = q + floor((s-t)*Rproj/Rsrc), inverse s(p) = t + floor((p-q)*Rsrc/Rproj), Lproj = len*Rproj//Rsrc: 1:1 involutivity over a full clip; boundary exactness (trim start to clip head, final sample to last project frame, one-past-end to first orphan position); 44.1k to 48k roundtrip failures 4516 of 4547 probes; new structure result: roundtrip succeeds if and only if the source offset is divisible by 147 (= 44100 / gcd(44100, 48000)); Lproj(441000) = 480000.\",\n      \"justified_expected_behavior\": \"At integer 1:1 ratio the mapping must be exactly involutive and boundary-exact; at 44100 to 48000 most samples cannot roundtrip, which is the documented justification for anchoring cues in source samples; the divisibility structure follows from gcd arithmetic.\",\n      \"stdout_summary\": \"A1 True; A2 head->2000 tail->6999 one-past-end->7000; B1 4516 of 4547; B2 True (period 147); C1 480000; FW1 OK.\",\n      \"corroboration\": \"Independently reproduces research-stage RW1 (4516/4547) and strengthens it with the mod-147 structure.\",\n      \"limits\": \"Pure integer arithmetic; no audio I/O, no libsndfile/libsamplerate, no application code. Proves properties of the proposed formula only.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FW2R1\",\n      \"name\": \"Timecode rule check rev 1 (disclosed failed-expectation receipt)\",\n      \"label\": \"disclosed_failure\",\n      \"execution_id\": \"exec-78dc_jg2\",\n      \"completed_utc\": \"2026-10-06T05:49:36Z\",\n      \"exit_code\": 0,\n      \"code_sha256\": \"cab563da3ba28bdf565bea1d909f4000ea75ce9bc8075b8f191713832dab2d48\",\n      \"stdout_sha256\": \"39de75100136ec210eebf2ad6b7e674ca73b8d72e13af26f7ff0c859f5d7da1b\",\n      \"scope\": \"Same formula as FW2; five expected constants in the check itself were wrong (half-second probe points mistaken for half-millisecond cases), so the output ends FW2 FAILED although the formula outputs shown were correct.\",\n      \"justified_expected_behavior\": \"Not applicable to the formula; retained to disclose the revision history per honest-labeling rules, mirroring the research stage's RW1 rev-1 disclosure.\",\n      \"stdout_summary\": \"5 FAIL lines all traced to wrong candidate expectations; formula behavior consistent with nearest-ms rounding.\",\n      \"limits\": \"Superseded by FW2 rev 2; kept as disclosure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FW2\",\n      \"name\": \"Display timecode rounding rule checks (rev 2)\",\n      \"label\": \"executed_by_candidate\",\n      \"execution_id\": \"exec-hg56emxu\",\n      \"completed_utc\": \"2026-10-06T05:50:25Z\",\n      \"exit_code\": 0,\n      \"code_sha256\": \"aaa798e402e35dbde313c0303d78d14551afb533e8220bc7e984da5c4d641ad6\",\n      \"stdout_sha256\": \"d4276683ec801472aedf9a915c05697e02f1893bc61143fb6a30b905a26ffa7f\",\n      \"scope\": \"ms = (p*1000 + rate//2) // rate with negative clamp: zero; single frame truncates to 0 ms; 24 frames at 48 kHz = exact half millisecond rounds UP to 1 ms; 23 frames stays 0; one frame under one second displays 01.000 (nearest-ms); half a second exactly 00.500; one frame before two hours ALSO displays 02:00:00.000 (C2 display property); negative clamps to 00:00:00.000; float pitfall preserved (2.675 formats as 2.67).\",\n      \"justified_expected_behavior\": \"The brief requires defined rounding and boundary behavior for displayed timecodes; nearest-ms half-up integer math is deterministic and the display-property case shows why timecodes must never be anchors.\",\n      \"stdout_summary\": \"11 PASS lines; FW2 OK (rev 2).\",\n      \"corroboration\": \"Consistent with research-stage RW2; adds the one-frame-before-two-hours display case.\",\n      \"limits\": \"Arithmetic-only isolated check; no GUI, playback, or export integration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FW3\",\n      \"name\": \"Size census, memory arithmetic, and cache-size correction\",\n      \"label\": \"executed_by_candidate\",\n      \"execution_id\": \"exec-w43eak5o\",\n      \"completed_utc\": \"2026-10-06T05:50:26Z\",\n      \"exit_code\": 0,\n      \"code_sha256\": \"ef47034d2bb6f24942725f9312a43d2c1869c9335a0bab23c3c10bbf5345c6c3\",\n      \"stdout_sha256\": \"2bea18319736fe95dbb7f0be3608c346894e87730449fbc1217b7736cbf4b011\",\n      \"scope\": \"2 h at 48 kHz = 345,600,000 frames; RIFF data-chunk bytes for 24-bit at 1/2/4/8 channels versus 4,294,967,295 (1,036,800,000 fits; 2,073,600,000 fits; 4,147,200,000 fits; 8,294,400,000 exceeds); whole-file float32 stereo footprint 2,764,800,000 bytes = 2.5749 GiB; 2 s stereo window 768,000 bytes = 750 KiB; corrected cache math: 1,350,000 min/max points at 256 spp = 5,400,000 bytes = 5.15 MiB; research-stage 6.7M-frame figure is 51.6x low.\",\n      \"justified_expected_behavior\": \"These constants size the export RF64 refusal boundary, the forbidden whole-file access pattern, the permitted window size, and the corrected per-source cache footprint (correction C1).\",\n      \"stdout_summary\": \"channels table with over-flag only at 8; whole-file 2.5749 GiB; window 750 KiB; corrected cache 5.15 MiB; FW3 OK.\",\n      \"corroboration\": \"Matches research-stage RW3 on every shared constant; corrects only proposal section 7.2's prose estimate, which RW3 had never asserted.\",\n      \"limits\": \"Arithmetic only; does not measure a real renderer or the libsndfile RF64 writer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FW4\",\n      \"name\": \"Join lengths and equal-power crossfade property\",\n      \"label\": \"executed_by_candidate\",\n      \"execution_id\": \"exec-tbwyokfw\",\n      \"completed_utc\": \"2026-10-06T05:50:46Z\",\n      \"exit_code\": 0,\n      \"code_sha256\": \"e43ebaf6b73cf516192c3d431c92b5fe4cc340fb9fee12c04faff99e3bfc60ba\",\n      \"stdout_sha256\": \"36da0f6575625718158d8b46676ee2cbff49af1c4f4b6199095b2eb93f916dda\",\n      \"scope\": \"Butt join length = lenA + lenB (240,000 frames); crossfade length = lenA + lenB - D (239,760 at D = 240); cos/sin equal-power ramps have power sum 1 across the fade within 1e-9; edge gains correct (1,0 to 0.0065, 1.0); worst-case in-phase full-scale peak through the fade is 1.414214.\",\n      \"justified_expected_behavior\": \"Equal-power definition implies unit power sum; the 1.414 in-phase peak justifies making the export clipping census mandatory (correction C5).\",\n      \"stdout_summary\": \"butt 240000; xfade 239760; power sum True; edges True; peak 1.414214; FW4 OK.\",\n      \"limits\": \"Formula-level only; no claim about perceived transition quality.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"RW1\",\n      \"name\": \"Research-stage mapping checks (adopted)\",\n      \"label\": \"adopted_research_stage_receipt\",\n      \"execution_id\": \"exec-skw8qxd4\",\n      \"origin\": \"frozen research catalog: inputs/prior/C-03-RESOURCE-R002-BUNDLE-treatment-research-a001/research/witnesses.json; includes disclosed rev-1 failure exec-dztmovzi\",\n      \"corroboration\": \"Independently reproduced by FW1 this stage (identical 4516/4547 and Lproj constant).\",\n      \"limits\": \"As stated in the research catalog: arithmetic only.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"RW2\",\n      \"name\": \"Research-stage timecode checks (adopted)\",\n      \"label\": \"adopted_research_stage_receipt\",\n      \"execution_id\": \"exec-y6407e0b\",\n      \"origin\": \"frozen research catalog (same path)\",\n      \"corroboration\": \"Consistent with FW2 rev 2; FW2 adds the display-property case.\",\n      \"limits\": \"Arithmetic only.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"RW3\",\n      \"name\": \"Research-stage RIFF/memory/window arithmetic (adopted)\",\n      \"label\": \"adopted_research_stage_receipt\",\n      \"execution_id\": \"exec-6qrpmckx\",\n      \"origin\": \"frozen research catalog (same path)\",\n      \"corroboration\": \"Independently reproduced by FW3 on every shared constant.\",\n      \"limits\": \"Arithmetic only.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"proposed_unexecuted_summary\": \"All implementation-stage validation (property tests, golden renders, interrupt and cancel simulations, memory soak, accessibility audit, format matrix, lossy-seek roundtrip, metadata retention, render-path separation) is PROPOSED/UNEXECUTED and enumerated in proposal.md section 11; no receipts exist for it in any stage.\"\n}"}, "leads.json": {"text_utf8": "{\n  \"schema\": \"er9.final.leads.v1\",\n  \"stage\": \"critic_final\",\n  \"leads\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L01\",\n      \"title\": \"OHMS (Oral History Metadata Synchronizer, University of Kentucky) as transcript-cue sync precedent\",\n      \"status\": \"unavailable_in_environment\",\n      \"detail\": \"Four fetch attempts have now failed at the tool boundary: research stage https://ohms.uky.edu/ (ValueError) and https://www.ohms.uky.edu/ (DNS); this stage repeated https://ohms.uky.edu/ at 2026-10-06T05:48Z (ValueError). No bytes captured, so no claim about OHMS internals is made. The mechanism-family rationale (sync metadata separate from media; timecode-indexed transcripts for oral history) remains a plausible lead for the cue data contract but is UNVERIFIED.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Retry from a permitted network path or use published OHMS documentation PDFs; do not cite until captured.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L02\",\n      \"title\": \"WebVTT timestamp/cue syntax sections (deep spec text)\",\n      \"status\": \"partially_captured\",\n      \"detail\": \"Re-captured this stage byte-identically (S18, sha a9425c5b...); still truncated at 524,288 bytes with body_complete=false, so the normative timestamp grammar and cue-identifier sections remain unread. WebVTT is used in the proposal as an opportunity only (10.1), never as a pinned syntax reference.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Range-read the editor's draft to pin the timestamp grammar before implementing the WebVTT cue exporter.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L03\",\n      \"title\": \"libsndfile bext (Broadcast Wave) command API\",\n      \"status\": \"resolved_command_level\",\n      \"detail\": \"RESOLVED this stage: S19 (command.html, docs version 1.2.2) pins SFC_GET_BROADCAST_INFO and SFC_SET_BROADCAST_INFO (Get/Set the Broadcast Chunk info), upgrading the research stage's believed-only status. Residual limitation: the field-level SF_BROADCAST_INFO struct section of the page was not range-read, so field-level semantics (coding history size limits and so on) are still unpinned. The proposal's metadata-retention design relies only on the generic chunk API [S12]; bext read via the command interface is a bounded addition.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Range-read the SFC_GET_BROADCAST_INFO section before implementing bext display or export.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L04\",\n      \"title\": \"EBU Tech 3306 (RF64) primary specification and libsndfile RF64 write path\",\n      \"status\": \"unfetched_with_new_pin\",\n      \"detail\": \"The EBU primary PDF was not fetched in any stage. NEW this stage: S19 pins SFC_RF64_AUTO_DOWNGRADE (auto downgrade from RF64 to WAV), so the export design must explicitly disable silent downgrade when the 32-bit RIFF field would overflow (proposal 3, 7.3). libsndfile's actual RF64 write-path behavior at 1.2.2 remains unverified.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Fetch and pin tech3306 if RF64 export becomes a requirement; verify the RF64 write path and the downgrade command's behavior at the pinned version.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L05\",\n      \"title\": \"audiowaveform upstream continuation on Codeberg\",\n      \"status\": \"adoption_caveat\",\n      \"detail\": \"S03 records that ongoing development moved to codeberg.org/chrisn/audiowaveform; all evidence here refers to the GitHub side (latest release v1.10.3, 2025-08-20, per S01/S02). Anyone adopting audiowaveform as a component must re-bind pins against the Codeberg continuation.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"If used as a component, pin the Codeberg release and re-verify the regression tests exist there.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L06\",\n      \"title\": \"BBC peaks.js browser waveform/zoom component\",\n      \"status\": \"deferred\",\n      \"detail\": \"Zoom/overview precedent (S03 shows audiowaveform targets peaks.js); browser-targeted, out of scope for a native desktop v1.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Consult peaks.js docs only if a web companion viewer is requested.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L07\",\n      \"title\": \"Alternative I/O pipelines: GStreamer; Rust (symphonia/cpal)\",\n      \"status\": \"deferred_alternatives\",\n      \"detail\": \"Bounded alternatives to libsndfile/libsamplerate for format reach and language choice; not investigated in any stage. The chosen stack keeps the audio core in the two pinned C libraries so UI and language remain separable.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Evaluate only if the v1 input set proves insufficient; each alternative needs its own release/API binding pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L08\",\n      \"title\": \"Local automatic transcription for draft cues\",\n      \"status\": \"optional_opportunity_unexecuted\",\n      \"detail\": \"The brief lists automatic transcription as optional. An offline local model could generate draft cues bound to the same source-anchor contract; nothing was executed or benchmarked.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Prototype only after the cue contract is stable; measure RAM and latency on the 8 GB target.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L09\",\n      \"title\": \"Single-file SQLite project format (Audacity AU3-style) as alternative container\",\n      \"status\": \"alternative_considered_deferred\",\n      \"detail\": \"S16 documents the .aup3 single-file shape and its costs (opaque to other tools, undo history not saved, WAL/SHM sidecars, 4 GB-class exchange friction). The proposal chooses a folder bundle with an atomic JSON manifest; the SQLite container remains the documented fallback (proposal 10.2), reusing SQLite's transactional discipline via S17 either way.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Re-evaluate if multi-editor merge or very many small objects make JSON manifests unwieldy.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L10\",\n      \"title\": \"Loudness measurement (EBU R128-class) and reviewed-region tracking\",\n      \"status\": \"deferred_opportunity\",\n      \"detail\": \"Loudness normalization is out of v1 scope per the brief; a peak and clipped-sample census per export is in scope (7.2, strengthened by FW4). Reviewed-region tracking remains the headline opportunity (10.1).\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Keep region-review state schema-forward; add R128 only with a proper meter implementation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"L11\",\n      \"title\": \"Lossy-codec seek offset (MP3 info frames / Opus pre-skip and pre-roll)\",\n      \"status\": \"open_risk\",\n      \"detail\": \"S02 shows audiowaveform corrected an MP3 initial offset (v1.1.0) and fixed an MP3 decoder buffer overflow (v1.5.1), evidencing that lossy input handling is a real defect class. libsndfile seek is frame-based (S12), but codec delay and padding at seek boundaries for MP3/Opus/Vorbis in 1.2.2 are unverified. Until the roundtrip test passes, lossy sources carry a provenance flag and the scrub cursor reports decoded positions.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Seek-to-frame versus sequential-decode roundtrip per lossy format at the pinned libsndfile; document discrepancies before sample-exact claims reach users.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}}}